# Emergency braking (docs/emergency_stop.md) on the burn-in axis (10 mm a
# revolution): at 188 rad/s (300 mm/s) something fails; hv0.sim_dist,
# zeroed then, is how far the axis went (1 rad = 1.59 mm). Coasting takes
# ~16 rad (26 mm) and ~180 ms.
# A quick stop after a lost link, and then the encoder fails too: the quick
# stop (it needs feedback) turns into the dynamic brake. The ms the fault
# filter takes run on the frozen encoder, so a little more than either alone.
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
@timeout 120
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 1.5
lcnc 1 300
run 1
hv0.sim_vel
hv0.sim_dist = 0
lcncstop
run 0.007
fault0.stop
enc_fb0.sim_fail = 1
run 0.003
fault0.stop
run 0.3
hv0.sim_dist
hv0.sim_vel
fault0.en_out
@expect fault0.stop[1] == 1
@expect fault0.stop[2] == 2
@expect hv0.sim_dist < 5
@expect hv0.sim_vel[2] ~ 0 0.5
@expect fault0.en_out == 0
